<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isa ibn Ali Al Khalifa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1848">1848</a>–<a href="/years/1932">1932</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isa ibn Ali Al <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a> was ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a> from 1869, when the British installed him after a period of civil war, until 1923. His reign saw Bahrain bound to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> by the exclusive agreements of 1880 and 1892. In 1923 the British, pressing for administrative reform, forced him to hand power to his son Hamad, though he kept the title until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isa-ibn-ali-al-khalifa.jpg" alt="Isa ibn Ali Al Khalifa" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous photographer between 1860-1923 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Isa_bin_Ali_Al_Khalifa_(1848_%E2%80%93_1932).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
